# command-local-test — Quick local QA (Pickleball Advanced Open Play)

> **Invoke:** Type `command-local-test`, `@command-local-test`, or "run local test" for the Open Play local-page site.

---

## Law

`Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/` is the only local test site source. Do not mirror staging/live into it unless Sam explicitly asks for a copy operation.

## Action

1. From the **Website** folder (`package.json` root), run:
   ```powershell
   npm run local-test
   ```
   This starts **live-server** on port **3456** and opens `/Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/index.html`. It does not copy files.

2. **Guard only** (no browser):
   ```powershell
   npm run local-test:sync
   ```
   This validates the local test site exists. It does not copy files.

---

## What gets served

The existing files under `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/`.

---

## Output

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/...` | Canonical local test site — **not** for deploy |

Do not regenerate this folder from staging/live during normal local development.

---

## URL (after `npm run local-test`)

Canonical path:

`http://127.0.0.1:3456/Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/index.html`

---

## Staging vs live (Open Play)

Local preview edits go to **`Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/`**. Firebase Hosting deploys **`Programs/Pickleball/live/`** only when Sam explicitly asks for production propagation/deploy.
